Make SyncBatchNorm._specify_ddp_gpu_num a no-op on PyTorch >= 2.0.

torch.nn.SyncBatchNorm._specify_ddp_gpu_num was an internal hook used to size
the DDP gradient buckets. It was folded into _ddp_init_helper and removed in
torch 2.0. mmcv 1.3.0 still overrides it and unconditionally delegates to
super(), so `norm_cfg=dict(type='SyncBN')` (the setting the benchmark configs
use) raises

    AttributeError: 'super' object has no attribute '_specify_ddp_gpu_num'

at model construction time, before any data is touched.

The override only existed to keep the parrots (non-torch) branch inert. Guard
the delegation on the parent actually having the hook, which keeps torch 1.x
behaviour identical and degrades to a no-op on torch 2.x, where the equivalent
work happens inside _ddp_init_helper anyway.

--- a/mmcv/utils/parrots_wrapper.py
+++ b/mmcv/utils/parrots_wrapper.py
@@ -83,7 +83,10 @@ class SyncBatchNorm(SyncBatchNorm_):

     def _specify_ddp_gpu_num(self, gpu_size):
         if TORCH_VERSION != 'parrots':
-            super()._specify_ddp_gpu_num(gpu_size)
+            # torch < 2.0 sizes the DDP gradient buckets here; from 2.0 on the
+            # equivalent logic lives in _ddp_init_helper and this hook is gone.
+            if hasattr(super(), '_specify_ddp_gpu_num'):
+                super()._specify_ddp_gpu_num(gpu_size)

     def _check_input_dim(self, input):
         if TORCH_VERSION == 'parrots':
